  (compare against the image-patch-only row in phase 2. Zeroing every traced head at the last token severs every path by which the patched image can reach that position after block 21, so cause here SHOULD fall to the unhooked floor. If it does not, either --blocks is too narrow or the read does not go through the last token's attention -- and that would be the finding.)

==============================================================================
=== phase 2: cumulative knockout under the image patch (path patching)
==============================================================================
  unhooked:                       cause=  0.0% base_kept=100.0%
  image patch only (k=0):         cause= 98.4% base_kept=  0.0%   <-- the effect being traced
  restore top-1   heads:            cause= 85.9% base_kept=  6.2%  (recovered 12.7% of the effect)
  restore top-2   heads:            cause= 75.0% base_kept= 18.8%  (recovered 23.8% of the effect)
  restore top-4   heads:            cause= 29.7% base_kept= 57.8%  (recovered 69.8% of the effect)
  restore top-8   heads:            cause=  0.0% base_kept= 90.6%  (recovered 100.0% of the effect)
  restore top-16  heads:            cause=  0.0% base_kept= 90.6%  (recovered 100.0% of the effect)
  restore 8 RANDOM heads (null):   cause= 85.9% base_kept=  6.2%

  top-8 vs random-8 gap: +85.9% of cause. A gap near zero means the phase-1 ranking is NOT carrying information and the curve above says nothing about which heads matter.

==============================================================================
=== phase 3: sufficiency -- patch ONLY these heads, no image patch
==============================================================================
  The mirror of phase 2. Instead of removing a head's contribution from a fully patched run, this INSTALLS it into an otherwise clean one: the image is NOT swapped, and the selected heads are forced to the values they took when it was. Necessity (phase 2) is the question redundancy breaks; sufficiency is not, so a small set reproducing the effect here is localization even if the knockout curve is flat.

  nothing patched (k=0):          cause=  0.0% base_kept=100.0%   <-- must match the unhooked row above
  ALL 84 traced heads:           cause= 85.9% base_kept=  3.1%   <-- a PARTIAL ceiling: downstream block(s) [24, 25, 26, 27] are not traced, so their attention still reads the clean image
  patch top-1   heads:              cause=  0.0% base_kept=100.0%  ( 0.0% of this arm's ceiling)
  patch top-2   heads:              cause=  1.6% base_kept= 93.8%  ( 1.8% of this arm's ceiling)
  patch top-4   heads:              cause= 31.2% base_kept= 54.7%  (36.4% of this arm's ceiling)
  patch top-8   heads:              cause= 84.4% base_kept=  3.1%  (98.2% of this arm's ceiling)
  patch top-16  heads:              cause= 87.5% base_kept=  1.6%  (101.8% of this arm's ceiling)
  patch 8 RANDOM heads (null):     cause=  0.0% base_kept=100.0%   <-- same heads as phase 2's null

  top-8 vs random-8: 84.4% vs 0.0% of cause.

==============================================================================
=== phase 4: shuffled-donor control (is the content row-specific?)
==============================================================================
  Each row is given the head outputs ANOTHER row's source flag produced, and scored against its own source gold (`own`), the donor's source gold (`donor`), and its base gold (`kept`). If these heads carry the source's identity, `own` must collapse and `donor` must rise. `own` staying high would mean the effect never depended on which image was patched in.
       top-8 shuffled:  own=  1.6% donor= 82.8% kept=  3.1%   (unshuffled cause was 84.4%)
      ALL 84 shuffled:  own=  1.6% donor= 89.1% kept=  1.6%   (unshuffled cause was 85.9%)

  -> CONFIRMED at top-8: rolling the donor moves the answer WITH it (own=1.6%, donor=82.8%), so these heads carry the source image's identity and the sufficiency result is about the model, not the plumbing. THIS k, not the smallest k whose phase-3 cause moved, is the localization number worth quoting.

